    "alert_id": "ALERT_TDF_MONITORING_GAP",
    "title": "Missing TDF renal and bone monitoring labs",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring for patients on TDF-containing regimens. The patient has been on TDF for 6 years, yet the clinician's plan does not include any renal function monitoring beyond today's creatinine. No eGFR was calculated, and no urine protein-to-creatinine ratio was ordered despite trace proteinuria on dipstick. Serum phosphate was checked today and found low (0.78 mmol/L) but was not addressed in the assessment or plan. A 6-month review interval without renal monitoring is inadequate given the abnormal phosphate and proteinuria findings.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Calculate eGFR, order urine protein-to-creatinine ratio, and repeat serum phosphate. Establish regular renal monitoring schedule per TDF guidelines rather than 6-month review without labs.",
    "citations": [
      {"page_number": 260, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p27_c2"},
      {"page_number": 270, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p37_c1"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_IBUPROFEN_TDF_NSAID",
    "title": "Ibuprofen plus TDF increases renal injury risk",
    "message": "Guidelines list acute kidney injury as a TDF toxicity and recommend renal function monitoring. The patient uses over-the-counter ibuprofen regularly for chronic back pain while on TDF. NSAIDs reduce renal perfusion and can potentiate TDF-induced tubular damage, compounding the risk of nephrotoxicity. The patient already has trace proteinuria and low serum phosphate, which may signal early renal tubular injury. The clinician's plan recommends PRN ibuprofen without flagging this interaction or advising renal monitoring. Alternative analgesia should be considered.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Counsel on minimizing ibuprofen use. Consider alternative analgesics (e.g., paracetamol) and monitor renal function closely given concurrent TDF and possible early tubulopathy.",
