      {"page_number": 270, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p37_c1"},
      {"page_number": 260, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p27_c2"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_EFV_AMLODIPINE_INTERACTION",
    "title": "EFV decreases amlodipine levels, contributing to poor BP",
    "message": "Guidelines state that efavirenz can potentially decrease dihydropyridine (amlodipine) drug levels, though no dose adjustment is required. The patient has suboptimal blood pressure (146/94) despite being prescribed amlodipine 5 mg, and admits to missed doses while travelling. The EFV-amlodipine interaction may contribute to reduced antihypertensive efficacy, compounding the adherence problem. The clinician attributed poor BP control solely to missed doses without considering the pharmacokinetic interaction. While no dose adjustment is mandated, awareness of this interaction is important if BP remains uncontrolled despite improved adherence.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "low",
    "recommended_action": "Reinforce amlodipine adherence. If BP remains elevated despite full adherence, consider dose increase or switch to an antihypertensive less affected by EFV induction.",
